{"id":903,"date":"2020-09-28T17:35:29","date_gmt":"2020-09-28T17:35:29","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?post_type=researcher&#038;p=903"},"modified":"2024-09-12T08:35:51","modified_gmt":"2024-09-12T08:35:51","slug":"kenneth-dadedzi","status":"publish","type":"researcher","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/researcher\/kenneth-dadedzi\/","title":{"rendered":"Dr. Kenneth Dadedzi"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover profile-banner bg-alt\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim-100 has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:none\"><\/span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n\n\n<a href=\"javascript:history.back()\"> <div class=\"profiles-btn\"> \n\n<div class=\"btn-left-sq bg-primary\"> <i class=\"fa fa-caret-left white-text\"> <\/i> <\/div>\n<div class=\"btn-text title-bold white-text\">Back to Profiles<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/a>\n\n<h2 class=\"profile-name\">Dr. Kenneth Dadedzi<\/h2>\n\n<p class=\"profile-info profile-tagline primary-bold prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>Spectral Graph Theory<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5 profile-body\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/kenneth.jpg\"\/>\n\n\n<p>Kenneth Dadedzi is originally from Ghana. He completed his undergraduate studies at the University of Cape Coast, Ghana, followed by a Masters and Ph.D degrees at the Stellenbosch University, South Africa.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>He was part of the African Institute for Mathematical Sciences (AIMS) South Africa 2013\/2014 intake.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The area of his research is in Spectral Graph Theory, which involves studying eigenvalues of matrices associated with graphs.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Ken is currently a tutor for the Taught Masters 2019\/2020 academic year at AIMS Ghana.<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered"